{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019geBaBT1fsiHhaBy3v5g1Z","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"The final decision in the Diskless Core design discussion was to build a new independent metadata component for diskless topics rather than reuse the existing RLMM.\\\\n\\\\n- 2026-05-12T18:28:49.000000Z - Jun Rao proposed (JR11) leaving the existing RLMM as is for classic topics and designing a new, more efficient metadata management component independent of RLMM, which would be the only metadata component diskless topics depend on. [mail:620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54]\\\\n- 2026-05-13T10:53:30.000000Z - Satish Duggana agreed (+1) with Jun's proposal, stating RLMM was not designed for aggressive copying of the latest data to tiered storage and supporting an efficient metadata management system for diskless topics. [mail:51a25dcd9861c2e258ab8f04]\\\\n- 2026-05-15T19:50:51Z - Jun Rao reaffirmed the decision in his final message, arguing that managing object metadata in two places (diskless coordinator and RLMM) is more complex than managing all metadata in a single component, and that reusing RLMM would require addressing issues like tiering multiple partitions in a single object and avoiding blind propagation of all metadata to every broker. [mail:a192cc3ce6018a685014966e]\\\\n\\\\nWhat could not be determined: Nothing; the decision is explicitly documented in the cited messages.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"mail:620fcc0982fad00dc9a0bd54\\\",\\\"mail:51a25dcd9861c2e258ab8f04\\\",\\\"mail:a192cc3ce6018a685014966e\\\",\\\"mail:eccf8894903dbc34be1145c8\\\",\\\"mail:48e929153846405ff3b22830\\\",\\\"mail:e4a05c90c512657787366663\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":100.906,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":17,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":null,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.00679289,\\\"input_tokens\\\":198841,\\\"output_tokens\\\":17355}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_i